---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalNav from '../components/LegalNav.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../config/site';

const description =
  'Appidge Terms of Service: license grant and trial, product nature (not a VPN, no nodes included), purchases via Creem as Merchant of Record, acceptable use, disclaimers, and limitation of liability.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service" description={description} path="/terms" locale="en">
  <div class="doc">
    <div class="container doc-layout">
      <LegalNav locale="en" current="terms" />
      <article class="prose doc-main">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <div class="doc-meta">
        <span><b>Effective</b> 2026-07-24</span>
        <span><b>Last updated</b> 2026-07-24</span>
        <span><b>Applies to</b> the Appidge macOS app and related services</span>
      </div>

      <p class="lede">
        By using or purchasing Appidge you agree to these terms. Pay particular attention to
        section 2 (what the product is), section 4 (Merchant of Record), and section 6
        (acceptable use).
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">1</span>Definitions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>“Software”</strong> means the Appidge macOS application, its components, and updates.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>“Operator”, “we”</strong> means the independent solo developer who builds and
          operates Appidge in a personal capacity (contact details in section 11).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>“License”</strong> means the purchased entitlement to use the Software's paid
          features under these terms.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>“Creem”</strong> means Creem (creem.io) — the Merchant of Record for this
          product; its legal entity name is as stated in Creem's own terms.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="num">2</span>What the product is — and is not</h2>
      <p>
        The Software is a <strong>process-level network forwarding utility that runs locally on
        your Mac</strong>: by the rules you set, it forwards each process's connections to a
        proxy service you configured yourself, or directly.
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <h3>The Software is not a VPN and includes no network service</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            We <strong>do not provide, sell, or resell</strong> any VPN, proxy nodes, servers,
            or traffic relay services.
          </li>
          <li>
            Your traffic <strong>never passes through our servers</strong>. The forwarding
            target is a proxy you choose and configure; its availability, legality, and
            security are between you and its provider.
          </li>
          <li>
            A license unlocks <strong>software features</strong>. It includes no network access
            or node service of any kind.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2><span class="num">3</span>License grant and trial</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The Software is free to download and try for a <strong>7-day trial, starting at first launch</strong>; the exact days remaining are shown in the app.</li>
        <li>
          Upon purchase you receive a <strong>non-exclusive, non-transferable</strong> license
          for use on up to the permitted number of devices; the activation limit is stated at
          checkout and in the product description.
        </li>
        <li>
          License keys are for your own use (or the entity named at purchase) and
          <strong>may not be resold, shared, or published</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          No reverse engineering, removal of technical protections, or circumvention of license
          validation, except where mandatory law permits.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="num">4</span>Purchases and Merchant of Record (Creem)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Purchases are completed through Creem's hosted checkout.
          <strong>Creem is the Merchant of Record</strong>: orders, invoices, taxes, and payment
          processing are handled by Creem under its
          <a href="https://www.creem.io/terms" rel="noopener">terms</a>; Creem is the party
          you pay and the name on your statement.
        </li>
        <li>Price, currency, and tax are as shown at checkout.</li>
        <li>
          The software license itself is granted by the Operator under these terms; payment
          disputes may also involve Creem's applicable policies.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="num">5</span>Refunds</h2>
      <p>
        Full refund within 14 days of purchase, no questions asked — details in the
        <a href="/refund">refund policy</a>. Once refunded, the corresponding license is
        deactivated.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">6</span>Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You must use the Software <strong>in compliance with the law of your jurisdiction</strong>.</li>
        <li>
          You set the rules and you choose the upstream proxy:
          <strong>you are fully responsible for your rule configuration, the proxy services you
          connect, and the network activity that results</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          No unlawful use of any kind — including unauthorized access to others' systems,
          distributing malware, or any network activity prohibited by law.
        </li>
        <li>Violations may lead to termination under section 10.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="num">7</span>Updates and service availability</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          We may ship updates from time to time (features and security fixes); significant
          changes are noted in release notes.
        </li>
        <li>
          License validation is provided on a <strong>commercially reasonable efforts</strong>
          basis. If the service is temporarily unreachable, the Software allows an offline
          grace period rather than locking paid features immediately.
        </li>
        <li>
          We don't promise perpetual compatibility with every third-party proxy or future
          macOS release, but we make reasonable efforts to keep mainstream setups working.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="num">8</span>Intellectual property and third-party trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        The Software and this site's content are the Operator's intellectual property.
        Proxifier, Clash, Surge, Docker, and other names mentioned here are trademarks of
        their respective owners, used only to indicate compatibility or category —
        <strong>Appidge is not affiliated with or endorsed by any of them</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">9</span>Disclaimers and limitation of liability</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The Software is provided <strong>“as is”</strong>. To the maximum extent permitted by
          law, no express or implied warranties are given (including merchantability or fitness
          for a particular purpose).
        </li>
        <li>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Operator is not liable for indirect
          losses, data loss, or business interruption; aggregate liability is capped at
          <strong>the amount you actually paid for the license</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Nothing here excludes liability that cannot be excluded under mandatory law, or
          limits your statutory rights as a consumer.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="num">10</span>Termination</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You may stop using the Software and deactivate your license at any time.</li>
        <li>
          On material breach (especially sections 3 and 6) we may terminate your license after
          notice; licenses terminated for abuse are not refunded unless the law requires
          otherwise.
        </li>
        <li>A completed refund terminates the license automatically.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="num">11</span>Changes, assignment, governing law, contact</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Material changes will be posted here with a new effective date; continued use after a
          change constitutes acceptance.
        </li>
        <li>
          If the Operator later forms a company or other entity to carry on the Appidge
          business, these terms may be assigned to that entity as a whole. An assignment does
          not reduce any rights you already have under these terms and will be announced on
          this page.
        </li>
        <li>
          These terms are governed by the law of <strong>the Operator's place of habitual
          residence</strong>. Disputes go first to good-faith negotiation by email; failing
          that, to the competent courts of that place. Mandatory consumer protection rules of
          your jurisdiction always prevail.
        </li>
        <li>
          Contact: <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> — it reaches the
          developer directly. Operator: Appidge, an independent solo-developer operation.
        </li>
      </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
